A||||27||batboy||Batmobile vs. Vette||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||06-03-2000||09:27 PM||||Well, going to Kansas City on the turnpike yesterday was interesting. I did a stupid thing and not only raced a Corvette, but I raced it twice. One loss and one win.<P>I was doing the speed limit on the turnpike when a blue C5(?) Vette rolled up beside me in the passing lane. I goosed the throttle a couple times, mainly because I wondered how a $4,000 Batmobile would do against a $40,000 sports car. No response. I paced him and punched it hard, pulled a car length and backed off. As he drew back up even with me, I heard him drop a gear and floor it. I was completely off the gas, not expecting him to do that at all. He pulled a half a car length before I got the 4 barrels opened up. He continued to pull ahead slightly until he had a full car length and we were rolling past 90 MPH. I backed off, knowing this was not a smart thing to be doing on an interstate highway. I lost, but that Vette didn't exactly run away from me, especially considering he had the edge.<P>I lost track of the Vette and several miles later I pulled up into the long lines of cars at the toll booths. When it was my turn, I looked over and was surprised to see the blue Vette at the booth next to me. I looked ahead and saw my lane ended about a 1000 yards ahead which forces you to merge to the next lane to the left, which of course was the Vette's lane. We both left the booths with me being a nose ahead as we headed back for open highway. I didn't hesitate this time, I nailed the pedal to the floor and left it there. I heard the Vette shift and then shift again. The wimp, he was only running it up to 3,500 RPM or so. I'm guessing he had a 5 speed or a 6 speed tranny. The Batmobile was pulling strong and when I got close to a two car length lead on him, I flash my turn signal to merge because I'm rapidly running out of lane. I see the Vette's nose drop down, YIPPEE, he backed off. I chalked this one up as a victory. I'm sure a better driver in the same car would of beat me though. Still, not a bad showing for a half finished V8 project Fiero. However, I resolved afterwards to never do that foolishness on the Turnpike again, that's like begging the troopers to arrest you. Not too smart.||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT Bastard||06-03-2000||10:27 PM||||Nice kill, Batboy!||||reg||14
Z||000002||Raydar||06-03-2000||11:16 PM||||I love it!!!<BR>I have this picture in my mind, of a very stock-looking silver SE doing a "smoke-boiling-from-the-wheelwells" launch, away from the tollgate. LOL!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>(Although I do recognize that it probably didn't happen that way.)<BR>Good Kill!||||reg||14
Z||000003||frontal lobe||06-04-2000||03:00 AM||||Way to go!  Man, out of the toll booth, he shouldn't even have been out of second gear, should he?||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||06-04-2000||09:17 AM||||No smokey burnouts, I launched only hard enough to barely chip the tires, once I felt it hook up, then I laid into it. I heard the Vette shift to second then to third before I got out ahead of him to the point I couldn't hear him anymore. He shifted WAY too early each time, but I could tell he had it floored in between shifts. I guess Vettes usually get left alone because of their reputation or something. After the toll booth incidence, the Vette hung way back and even though I settled back down to the speed limit, he never attempted to pass me again...hehehe.||||reg||1
