Z||000017||batboy||06-06-2000||07:50 PM||||Well, not being a Vette guy, I was not 100% sure it was a C5. After looking at some pics, I'm now positive it was a C5. The pic below shows a C4 and a C5 together. The one I raced was definitely a C5 Vette not the C4.<P>I have to laugh at the "bench racers" who won't believe a V8 Fiero, driven by a guy who has been racing since the 70's, whipped an overrated C5 Vette driven by some middle age wussy who probably never owned a high performance car before until now.<P>I looked up the specs. The C5 weighs about 500 lbs. more than my Batmobile, even though it probably has 140 hp more (at 5600 rpm). Torque is only about 50 ft/lbs more than my car. Take into account that he was shifting at 3,500 to 4,000 max, he was a very long ways from reaching that top hp figure. So maybe he had only about 50-75 hp difference over me. Using a 1/4 mile calculator puts us pretty close to even for ET.<P>From a standing start, torque rules, not horsepower. He has a little more torque, but also has more weight. It all evens out. If he don't know how to shift fast or was sloppy on one shift, then I have the advantage. Additionally, I was leading by a nose when we jumped on it. Another advantage to me. These Vettes are not invincible (except maybe the ZR-1 version) and I do believe I just proved it. Hehehe!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.vettepics.com/images/95/95and98_small.jpg"> ||||reg||1
