Z||000023||Dan86gt3.8||06-07-2000||11:00 PM||||glad to see some people realiuzed corvettes are nothing more than a expensive show off item.  the c4's are imo ugly and pretty slow.  And the new c5's aren't that much more impresive.  I saw one get beat by a 89 iroc on some nitto's.  That was a on a vette short block, 305 heads and tpi intake.  Anyways vettes are no where close to invinsible.  I would fear a ls1 z28 auto that had a stall and some drag radials.  I guess I will bring my experience up once more and swaer on a stack of ten bibles my friend in a 98 T/A will run right beside a vette and hes raced several different c5's both 6 speeds and autos.  They even have dynos that show f-bod's compared to vettes with identical hp&torque curves on the same dyno under same conditions.  Anyways I guess I am through ranting about vettes being not that great.  I still wish I had a supercharged 3.8 for that time this assmaster in a c5 said he'd race me for $1,000.  This is the same idiot that roled into the local cruising parking lott and said he'd race anybody for $50.  Well a lt1 96 camaro that has the right mod's was an auto and had a good stall converter in it agreed.  Well they went to a nearby street that was deserted and went from a light.  The vette spun at the line and patrick just launched like the space shuttle and got the guy by some 8 car lengths.  If I had a v8 fiero or a northstar fiero I would have gladly done the same thing to him.  Just because you spend 40-50k doesen't mean you are going to be fast!  <BR>Ohhh by the way 87 pegasus what kind of engine do you have, and are you estimating the 285 horsepower or did you dyno?<BR>But I bet batboy knows what I am talking about there are a few vette owners that run thier cars but most are yuppies that want to show off and thier cars will never see the other side of 4 grand on the tach.  I feel it a shame to do such a thing, but then again thats just me.||||reg||1
