Z||000025||batboy||06-08-2000||12:30 AM||||I have declined a few races with Vettes, one was a L88 Stingray...now those are awesome. The guy I bought my 454 short block from, he SCCA races an early 70's Vette with a maxed out big block and full race suspension. That's another one I'll never tangle with. There are plenty of C5's out there that have been modified and are driven by guys that know what they're doing. But most are owned by older guys having a mid-life crisis or rich kids that don't know how to drive. I just can't see buying a car that costs more than my house, when I can have a Vette killing Fiero for a small fraction of the price.||||reg||1
